From 3505ab884f967183a11c6596a597db0a6fcb9395 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Kaminski MVP <Kevin.Kaminski@bighatgroup.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:50:16 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(full-compaction): run the prune before any summary and
 report the mode

When a validated prune decision rides on the compaction task, the
compaction service now applies it right after the pre-compaction hooks:
abort checks bracket the synchronous apply, errors are logged and fall back
to the built-in summary with the fallback mentioned in the prune note, and
a recount decides the outcome. If the pruned context no longer blocks the
next turn, compaction finishes in prune mode with no model request at all;
otherwise the summary loop runs over the pruned history and the result is
marked prune_then_summary, with the prune record ordered before the
compaction record on the wire.

CompactionResult carries the mode, the dropped and truncated counts, and
the optional prune note everywhere a result is reported: the TUI notice
branches on the mode, the PostCompact hook payload gains mode,
dropped_calls, and truncated_results, telemetry compaction_finished gains
the same three optional fields, and the full_compaction.complete durable
record stores them (optionally, so older wires still replay). The TUI
compaction block, the resume transcript, the replay fold, the kap-server
event schemas, and the klient contract schema all understand the new
fields. Docs (en and zh) describe the /compact prune flow and the
PostCompact payload.
